Topi Linkala wrote:
> One comment. The commands are normally lower case letters. So hjkl and
> yubn is basic movement.

I'm aware of this, but figured since this one is most useful to people
who have never played roguelikes before, people who are likely to be
scared away if I wasn't careful, I decided to break with that tradition
and use a more readable convention, and explictly say "Shift", "Ctrl"
or "Alt" when modifier keys are needed.  (And say "Alt" instead of
"Meta.")  In later columns, if commands come up, I'll probably use the
more traditional style with a note explaining it.

